CALL newPutForth(804, 1, 'Wealth determines competitive outcomes in sports before a game is played. Rich schools get better facilities, better coaches, better recruiting budgets. The playing field is structurally unlevel, and pretending otherwise ignores how competition actually works.');
CALL newPutForth(883, 1, 'March Madness is the best sporting event in the world. Sixty-eight teams, single elimination, three weeks. No other format produces upsets, cinderella stories, and bracket chaos at that scale. It\'s the most democratic tournament in major sports.');
CALL newPutForth(884, 1, 'Single elimination is variance-maximizing by design. The best team in the country loses in the first round sometimes. That\'s not a flaw — it\'s the feature that makes March Madness what it is. But it does mean the best team rarely wins.');
CALL newPutForth(886, 1, 'Any program in Division I can win the NCAA tournament. That\'s not just theory — mid-majors make deep runs regularly. The tournament structure gives Butler and Gonzaga the same bracket format as Duke. That matters.');
CALL newPutForth(887, 1, 'Sixty-eight teams out of 350-plus Division I programs make the field. That\'s a selective cut. The tournament is inclusive by major sports standards but not truly open — the structure still favors power conference programs.');
CALL newPutForth(888, 1, 'Upsets in March Madness are common enough to be expected, not exceptional. High seeds get bounced early every year. The format makes that structurally inevitable, and that\'s why filling out a bracket is its own national sport.');
CALL newPutForth(889, 1, 'Low seeds rarely win the whole tournament. The format creates upsets in early rounds but tends to sort itself out as you advance. Survival through six games heavily favors talent and depth. Cinderella makes the Elite Eight; she rarely wins it all.');
CALL newPutForth(890, 1, 'Villanova\'s 1985 run as an 8 seed — beating Georgetown in the championship — remains the lowest seed to ever win the NCAA tournament. It\'s a genuine outlier that proves the format can produce miracles while also being the only such miracle in 40 years.');
CALL newPutForth(891, 1, 'Historically, the Final Four is dominated by top-four seeds. Only seven teams seeded fifth or lower have made the championship game in the tournament\'s modern era. The format has magic, but it still heavily rewards talent.');
CALL newPutForth(905, 1, 'American football is the best sport. The chess-like complexity of the formations, the physical demands across wildly different positions, the way individual brilliance interacts with team execution — no other sport does all of that simultaneously.');
CALL newPutForth(907, 1, 'More football exposure means more CTE exposure. That\'s not a political claim — it\'s the documented biology of repeated head trauma. The evidence is too strong at this point to treat it as contested.');
CALL newPutForth(930, 1, 'Baseball is a cherished American tradition, and I mean that without irony. The rhythm of the game, the way it stretches across a summer, the connection to history — baseball is woven into American identity in a way no other sport is.');
CALL newPutForth(932, 1, 'Of all the major sports, only NASCAR has athletes who cover less ground under their own power. A baseball outfielder jogs to his position, stands there, and occasionally sprints 90 feet. The athleticism is real but distributed extremely unevenly across a game.');
CALL newPutForth(935, 1, 'Serena Williams is the greatest athlete of all time. Twenty-three Grand Slam singles titles. Dominance across four decades. Performing at the top of her sport through injury, illness, and childbirth. The argument for anyone else requires ignoring that record.');
CALL newPutForth(937, 1, 'Great teammates make you better. A point guard who finds the open man, a wide receiver who commands double coverage, a center fielder who covers for his corners — elite teammates expand your game in ways you can\'t replicate alone.');
CALL newPutForth(939, 1, 'Baseball is uniquely suited to radio. The pace of the game works with narration rather than against it. A great baseball broadcaster can carry an entire afternoon game on voice alone. No other major sport transfers to audio as well.');
CALL newPutForth(943, 1, 'Women\'s sports deserve equal respect. The level of competition, the athletic achievement, the dedication required — none of that is lesser because the athletes are women. Treating women\'s sports as second-tier is a choice, not a natural outcome.');
CALL newPutForth(950, 1, 'Women\'s sports generate less viewership and revenue than the male equivalent in most sports right now. That\'s a market reality. It\'s also a self-fulfilling prophecy — less investment, less promotion, less visibility produces less audience.');
CALL newPutForth(951, 1, 'On average, men are larger, faster, and stronger than women. That\'s not an opinion — it\'s documented across athletic performance data. It\'s why sports are sex-segregated, and why the segregation makes athletic competitions meaningful.');
CALL newPutForth(952, 1, 'Women\'s sports currently generate less revenue than men\'s sports in most markets. That fact is descriptive, not prescriptive. It doesn\'t mean women\'s sports deserve less investment — it means the investment gap itself is partly causing the revenue gap.');
CALL newPutForth(1539, 1, 'Golf courses consume enormous quantities of land — land that in most cities could house thousands of people, support businesses, or serve as public parks. The exclusivity of what goes on that land compounds the problem.');
CALL newPutForth(1540, 1, 'The environmental cost of a golf course — the chemical inputs, the water consumption, the habitat displacement — is significant for an activity that serves a small fraction of the population. That\'s a poor trade for land that could preserve or restore nature.');
CALL newPutForth(1541, 1, 'Golf\'s core skills — ball striking, putting, course management — can be tested on a fraction of the acreage a traditional course requires. Simulation technology and smaller-format courses prove that. The full 18-hole format is tradition, not necessity.');
CALL newPutForth(1542, 1, 'Multiple tee boxes on any hole create meaningfully different challenges — different angles, different distances, different landing zones. What looks like the same hole plays like a different hole depending on where you start.');
CALL newPutForth(1544, 1, 'Golf courses occupy prime real estate — waterfront land, city-adjacent parcels, scenic locations — and bar virtually everyone from using it. The public subsidy many courses receive while excluding the public is particularly hard to justify.');




